# MUSZKA-MAMUTA — agent rules

You are modifying a fork of `cobanov/fly-connectome-template` (React 18, TypeScript strict, Three.js, Vite, Vitest).
Goal: a browser simulation where a *Drosophila melanogaster* with a MaleCNS v1.0-driven spiking brain eats a wedge
of Polish farmer's cheese ("twaróg klinek") for eternity, in the visual style of the viral "fly brain" reels
(dark grid → kitchen table, side HUD, view switcher).

## Non-negotiables

1. NEVER invent neuron body IDs, cell-type names or synapse counts. Every ID used in code must be loaded from the
   MaleCNS v1.0 export in `data/raw/` or from `public/data/brain-atlas/`. If you need a cell type (sugar GRNs, MN9),
   write a data-prep script that looks it up by annotation and emits JSON with provenance. If lookup fails, STOP and
   report — do not guess, do not substitute a plausible-sounding name.
2. MaleCNS bulk files are Apache Arrow Feather. Read with `pd.read_feather` / `pyarrow`. They are NOT CSV.
3. Keep the model boundary explicit: the brain simulation outputs `ActivityFrame` (existing template contract).
   Body animation and the twaróg system consume it; they never write into it.
4. Preserve `src/components/Attribution.tsx` and the README credit line ("Built with fly-connectome-template by
   Mert Cobanov"). MaleCNS stays CC BY 4.0, Flybody Apache-2.0. Add a "Methods" panel stating honestly what is
   measured (connectome graph, synapse signs) and what is authored (LIF params, hunger, food chemistry, every
   frame of motion).
5. UI text is Polish with an English toggle. Code, comments, commit messages in English.
6. Performance budget: 60 fps on M1/RTX 3060 at 1080×1920 with ≤ 20k simulated neurons. Heavy loops run in a Web
   Worker or WASM, never on the main thread.
7. Every phase ends with `npm run lint && npm test && npm run build` passing. Add tests for new logic.
8. No backend, no database, no auth, no analytics, no paid SDKs. Static site only.
9. Before large edits, print a short plan and the list of files you will touch. After edits, print a summary and
   manual verification steps.
10. Work in small commits with conventional-commit messages. Never amend or force-push.

## Domain cheat-sheet (VERIFY against MaleCNS annotations before using any name)

- Sweet gustatory receptor neurons (GRNs): Gr64f / Gr5a class, labellar (labial nerve) and tarsal; axons terminate
  in the subesophageal zone (SEZ).
- Second-order sugar interneurons: G2N-1, IN1 (SEZ). Feeding command: Fdg.
- Proboscis motor neurons: MN9 (rostrum protractor = proboscis extension), MN11/MN12 (haustellum), pharyngeal
  pump MNs. Shiu et al., Nature 2024 reproduced sugar GRN → MN9 in a LIF model. This is our ground truth.
- Bitter GRNs (Gr66a) suppress feeding. Amino-acid / yeast sensing: Ir76b class.
- Twaróg profile: protein-rich, mildly sour, very low sugar → drive comes mostly from amino-acid and olfactory
  channels, not sweet. Document this as an authored assumption.
- Hunger is NOT in the connectome: model it as neuromodulatory gain (AKH raises it, DSK/insulin lower it) applied
  to GRN→interneuron weights and to the MN9 threshold.